087f2"/></fig><fig id="f3-bmi-2006-087" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p><bold>C-reactive protein (CRP) response at study inclusion and after 4 to 6 weeks on treatment.</bold> In study I mean CRP levels decline from 47.8 mg/dl (standard deviation 40.4 mg/dl) to 37.5 mg/dl (standard deviation 37.2 mg/dl), p = 0.33, in study II from 40.1 (standard deviation 38.0) to 4.9 (standard deviation 3.9 mg/dl), p = 0.0005. The mean initial CRP levels of cohort I and II were not significantly different, p=0.63.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="bmi-2006-087f3"/></fig><table-wrap id="t1-bmi-2006-087" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Patient characteristics Study I and Study II.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th colspan="2" align="center" rowspan="1"><italic>STUDY I n = 18</italic></th><th colspan="2" align="center" rowspan="1"><italic>STUDY II n = 33</italic></th></tr><tr><th colspan="5" align="left" rowspan="1"><hr/></th></tr><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Characteristics</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">No.</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">%</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">No.</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">%</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td colspan="5" align="left" rowspan="1">Age, years</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Median</td><td colspan="2" align="center" rowspan="1">66</td><td colspan="2" align="center" rowspan="1">64</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Range</td><td colspan="2" align="center" rowspan="1">(53 &#x02013; 85)</td><td colspan="2" align="center" rowspan="1">(48 &#x02013; 78)</td></tr><tr><td colspan="5" align="left" rowspan="1">Sex</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Male</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">13</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">72</td><td align="center" rows